### 2. No security headers (OWASP A05: Security Misconfiguration)

Express sends an `X-Powered-By: Express` header (fingerprinting) and no protective headers (HSTS, CSP, `X-Content-Type-Options`, etc.).

**Recommendation:** Use `helmet` and disable the powered-by header.

```js
const helmet = require('helmet');
app.disable('x-powered-by');
app.use(helmet());
```

### 3. No rate limiting (OWASP A04 / A07)

All endpoints are open to unlimited requests, enabling brute force, scraping, and DoS.

